---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Replay Pact interactions against a provider and compare its responses

Usage: rustman contract pact verify [OPTIONS] --provider-url <URL> <PACT_FILE>...

Arguments:
  <PACT_FILE>...
          The Pact files to verify

Options:
      --provider-url <URL>
          The provider's base URL, as in http://localhost:8080

      --provider-states-url <URL>
          The provider's state-change endpoint; each provider state is POSTed to it before (setup) and after (teardown) its interaction

      --allow-mutations
          Replay POST, PUT and PATCH interactions

      --allow-destructive
          Replay DELETE interactions

      --production <HOST>
          Confirm a production provider by repeating its exact host

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Also write the report as json, junit, markdown, html or sarif, to a file or stdout, as in junit=out/pact.xml (repeatable)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment whose secret values are redacted from the output (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory, for [safety] and redaction (default: search from the current directory upwards; verification needs none)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
